    "desc": "Step-by-step guide to using save states in browser-based GBA emulators. Never lose progress again.",
    "date": "2026-08-25",
    "category": "Guides",
    "body": "<main style=\"max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px\">\r\n  <a href=\"/blog\" style=\"color:#c4a35a;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px\">← Back to Blog</a>\r\n  <span style=\"color:#555;font-size:12px;margin-left:12px\">2026-08-25</span>\r\n\r\n  <h1 style=\"font-size:2rem;margin:16px 0 8px\">How to Save Your GBA Game Progress in Browser</h1>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#aaa;margin-bottom:24px\">Step-by-step guide to using save states in browser-based GBA emulators. Never lose progress again.</p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">One of the best features of browser-based GBA emulators is <strong>save states</strong>. Unlike the original hardware where you needed a battery-backed cartridge, browser emulators let you save your exact position at any moment.</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">What Are Save States?</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">A save state is a snapshot of the emulator's exact memory state. It saves everything — your position, health, inventory, and even the frame of animation. This is different from in-game saves, which only work at save points.</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">How to Save on EggerMath</h2>\r\n  <ol style=\"padding-left:20px;color:#ccc;margin-bottom:24px\">\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Start playing any game on <a href=\"/\" style=\"color:#c4a35a\">EggerMath</a></li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Click the <strong>Save</strong> button in the toolbar (or press <strong>F5</strong>)</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Choose a slot (1-10) — slots with timestamps already have saves</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Click <strong>Save</strong> on the slot you want to use</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Your progress is saved to your browser's local storage</li>\r\n  </ol>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">How to Load a Save</h2>\r\n  <ol style=\"padding-left:20px;color:#ccc;margin-bottom:24px\">\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Click the <strong>Load</strong> button (or press <strong>F7</strong>)</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Select the slot with your save</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Click <strong>Load</strong> — you'll be back exactly where you left off</li>\r\n  </ol>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">10 Save Slots</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">EggerMath gives you 10 save slots per game, just like PPSSPP. This means you can:</p>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;color:#ccc;margin-bottom:24px\">\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Keep multiple playthroughs</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Save before boss fights</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Try different choices without losing progress</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Share saves with friends</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>\r\n  <div style=\"background:#111;border:1px solid #1e1e22;border-radius:8px;padding:16px;margin-bottom:24px\">\r\n    <p style=\"color:#ccc;font-family:monospace;margin-bottom:4px\"><strong style=\"color:#c4a35a\">F5</strong> — Open Save Menu</p>\r\n    <p style=\"color:#ccc;font-family:monospace;margin-bottom:4px\"><strong style=\"color:#c4a35a\">F7</strong> — Open Load Menu</p>\r\n    <p style=\"color:#ccc;font-family:monospace;margin-bottom:4px\"><strong style=\"color:#c4a35a\">F9</strong> — Quick Save to Slot 1</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">Tips</h2>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;color:#ccc;margin-bottom:24px\">\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Saves are stored in your browser — clearing cookies will delete them</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Use different slots for different situations (exploring, boss fights, etc.)</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">Save states work even if the game doesn't have in-game saves</li>\r\n    <li style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">You can have saves for multiple games at the same time</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <div style=\"margin-top:32px;padding:20px;background:#111;border:1px solid #1e1e22;border-radius:12px\">\r\n    <h2 style=\"font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:8px\">Try It Now</h2>\r\n    <p style=\"color:#aaa;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:12px\">Pick a game and try the save state feature yourself.</p>\r\n    <a href=\"/\" style=\"color:#c4a35a;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700\">Browse Games →</a>\r\n  </div>\r\r\r\n</main>",
